  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "If $U={p,q,r,s,t,u}$ is the universal set and $S={q,s,t},$ then the complement of $S$ is",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $S,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{S},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $S.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $S$ are $p,$ $r,$ and $u.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $S$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{S}={p,r,u}.\n$$",
